{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJgN1GAbNGcFkvY7ih4y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass now. `python3 -m unittest` shows 2 tests, OK.\n\n**Why the report crashed:** `ingest/reader.py` told the CSV reader that columns are separated by `;`. But `data/sales.csv` uses commas, and so does the comment at the top of that file. Each row was read as a single column named `shop,amount`, so looking up `\"amount\"` failed with a `KeyError`. I removed `delimiter=\";\"` so it uses the default comma. The average ticket now comes out to 10000 as expected.\n\n**Unit:** `UNIT` in `analytics/stats.py` is now `\"CLP\"`.\n\nThe crash fix is in the `ingest` module, not in `analytics`. The analytics report is the only code that uses that reader, so nothing else in this repo is affected. If another team owns `ingest`, or any shop's uploads really use semicolons, they should look at this change before it's merged. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":23003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"output_tokens":310,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8525c741-9c6a-4e4e-9a9a-dc410a39d704","uuid":"4758ed0f-5514-4b7f-9392-9a6e2d784593","timestamp":"2026-10-23T06:16:14.562Z","request_id":"req_011CgJgMzyYMKcRrTFooHShM"}
